{
 "about": "Vectors for the x402/upto/xrpl pairing (the x402-upto-xrpl entry point of @integraledger/lcp), x402's upto scheme on the XRP Ledger (specs/schemes/upto/scheme_upto_xrpl.md at x402-foundation/x402 88b66dd4, cited by line as :N). No published software implements the scheme (@x402/xrpl 2.30.0 ships exact alone), so every value is computed from the scheme's text by independent tools: fixed.O and fixed.OSettle are the scheme's own examples (:110-124, :128-142), verbatim. The keys are Ed25519 by XRPL's key derivation (xrpl.org, Cryptographic Keys, Ed25519 Key Derivation: the private key is SHA-512Half of 16 bytes of entropy, the public key 0xED and the curve point), entropy 01x16 the payer, 03x16 another account, 04x16 another destination, the account base58check of 0x00 and RIPEMD-160(SHA-256(public key)) (@noble/hashes 2.4.0 legacy, ripple-binary-codec 2.11.0's AccountID). create.txJson is written by hand from xrpl.org's PaymentChannelCreate fields; create.blob is ripple-binary-codec 2.11.0's encode with SigningPubKey and TxnSignature, the signature @noble/curves 2.4.0's Ed25519 over ripple-binary-codec's encodeForSigning; each hash is SHA-512Half of TXN\\0 and the blob (node:crypto). Each channel id is the PayChannel ID format (xrpl.org, PayChannel, PayChannel ID Format; :56): node:crypto's SHA-512Half of 0x0078, the two AccountIDs and the sequence or ticket, big-endian. claim.expect is ripple-binary-codec 2.11.0's encodeForSigningClaim({channel, amount}), the bytes :251-254 state, and claim.signature the payer's Ed25519 signature over them, which fixed.P presents. Expected answers of status are written by hand from the profiles read-status and x402-upto-xrpl, each row read on a constructed server holding ledgers 1 to 1001, 1000 validated, unless complete says otherwise (test/fixtures/xrpl-reader.ts): the reference of fixed.P with the row's channel, plus fromLedger 950, read for the act payment at the mark validated after the position 950. ledger_entry answers the row's PayChannel at the validated ledger, or entryNotFound where the row names none; account_tx answers the row's creates for the row's opener alone, each with tesSUCCESS at its ledger, validated unless the row says otherwise, its metadata creating the row's channel unless metadata is false. Refusal rows change one member of fixed.P or of fixed.O, as a JSON Pointer (RFC 6901) and its value, or remove it; their codes have no outside oracle and are the profile's rules 5 and 7 over the scheme's members (:144-150, :172-188, :236-243).",
